    "lastCommit": {
      "id": "e9a24a05f4af13cd464e35e5b41bb3e44ffb9cb4",
      "message": "OTA-1871 \u2014 the fixture must typecheck too\n\nCI 2261 failed one required job on 7e200c0f: `typecheck (tests \u00b7 ratchet)`,\n211 > baseline 196. All fifteen errors were in the suite shipped with OTA-1871.\nThe other seven required families were green \u2014 typecheck source, lint, source\ngates and all four fast shards \u2014 so the pin itself was never implicated, and\nproduction is byte-identical to 7e200c0f (`git diff 7e200c0f -- app/` is empty).\n\nWHY THE LOCAL RUN MISSED IT. The gate was run as `npm run -s typecheck:tests |\ntail -8; echo \"EXIT=$?\"`, which reports the exit status of `tail` \u2014 always 0.\nThe errors were printed and read as ordinary ratchet noise. Re-run without the\npipe, the same tree exits 1. That is a reporting defect in how the check was\ninvoked, not a new failure: the gate had been red since the suite was written.\n\nTWO CLASSES, BOTH FIXED AT SOURCE. The baseline is NOT moved.\n\n1. `kind: 'material'` is not a member of the InventoryItem kind union\n   (relic / weapon / armor / consumable / misc / runecaster / dog_armor). It was\n   never how the data works either: catalog materials carry NO `kind` field at\n   all \u2014 materials.json has none \u2014 and reach the Materials section through the\n   tag heuristic at the end of categorizeItem. The fixture now models them that\n   way, `kind: undefined`, which makes the KIND axis MORE faithful rather than\n   less: '' still sorts before the coin's 'misc', so that axis still buries the\n   coin without the pin, which is the whole point of the population.\n\n2. Indexed reads under the no-unchecked-index rule \u2014 `section[0].name` and the\n   RARITY_RANK lookups. Asserted non-null in the same style the suite next door\n   uses (ota1731's `menu0[0]!.result`), and the rarity rank extracted to a\n   helper with an explicit `?? 0`.\n\nEvery claim the suite makes is unchanged; no assertion was weakened or removed\nto reach green. ota1871 32/32 still, and the inverted-rank negative control\nstill takes it 13 red with production restored byte-for-byte (md5 e728b930).\n\nVerified with real exit codes this time: ratchet \"OK \u2014 at baseline (196). No\ngrowth\", typecheck source 0, lint 0, 22/22 check gates, full fast surface\n1369/1369 suites \u00b7 15,818 passed \u00b7 3 skipped, exit 0.\n\nThe OTA stamp is unchanged at 2026-09-22-1871: this commit adds no suite, so the\nhighest otaNNNN suite is still ota1871 and check:otastamp holds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
